    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17867" root="زفر" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَرٌ</span></b>  <i>A prop</i> of a tree. (K, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  [In modern
Arabic, it means <i>Grease, greasy food,</i> or <i>flesh-meat:</i> app. from the Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَرْ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفْر</span>, signifying
“ filth: ” and hence, <i>obscenity.</i> Hence also the
vulgar epithet <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفِر</span> (app. for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفِرٌ</span>), meaning <i>Greasy:</i>
and <i>foul,</i> or <i>filthy:</i> and <i>obscene.</i> See 5.]

